# @cast — the loss-aware peer-to-peer substrate-to-substrate translation
# prism.
#
# The recognition (2026-08-20, Alex → Reed): mirror-metaphor for what
# @cascade was too linear to hold. Cast-a-beam (optical, mirror-adjacent).
# Cast-as-CS-word (type-casting, actor-casting). Cast-a-spell (magic-
# adjacent, ties to @magic Foerster-gauge). Cast-a-mold (content-address-
# adjacent). Multi-valent without ambiguity. Alex 2026-08-20 verbatim:
# *"How about @cast? That works for both the beam-of-light mirror
# metaphor and is the computer science word."*
#
# What @cast IS at Rec #91 altitude: the peer-to-peer translation mesh
# BETWEEN facets, composing `@glue` (bridging primitive; LANDED at
# `shards/glue.mirror` 43.5KB) + `@fate` (inference primitive; LANDED
# at `shards/fate.mirror` 42.5KB) under the hood. @facet handles the
# radial projection FROM 𝓜 onto target Hilbert-carriers (generation
# surface); @cast handles the mesh BETWEEN target-substrates preserving
# Foerster-gauge as far as it can, measuring loss where it must.
#
# Mirror-metaphor architecture: one stone (𝓜), many facets (radial via
# @facet), mesh between facets (@cast). Together they dissolve @cascade's
# linear-waterfall metaphor by making the architecture non-linear-mesh.
# @cascade is architecturally superseded post-composition; the 47 shard
# files + 275+ occurrences that reference @cascade migrate through the
# Phase 3 rename cascade to the @facet + @cast decomposition.
#
# === composition-shape: @glue bridging + @fate inference ===
#
# @cast composes two landed primitives under the hood:
#   1. @glue provides the bridging semantics between two named
#      substrates (fold_back-style per `shards/glue/fold_back.mirror`
#      50.9KB; the substrate-decl for how one substrate's shape gets
#      folded onto another's).
#   2. @fate provides the inference-driven translation-selection
#      (tournament-style per `shards/fate/tournament.mirror` 51.5KB;
#      the substrate-decl for how candidate translations get
#      arbitrated). Not hardcoded translation-tables; inference-driven.
#
# Together: `@cast/X/Y` species declare translation FROM substrate X
# TO substrate Y with @glue.fold_back(X, Y) supplying the bridging
# semantics + @fate.tournament(candidates) arbitrating loss-optimal
# translations. Loss measurement per Rec #87 @attension Shannon-loss-
# min discipline (universal bidirectional projection operator with
# @magic gauge-preservation).
#
# === peer-to-peer mesh, not linear waterfall ===
#
# @cascade's failure was collapsing two orthogonal concerns into one
# tiered surface: (i) radial projection FROM 𝓜 onto multiple target
# Hilbert-carriers, and (ii) peer-to-peer translation BETWEEN target
# substrates. These are at right angles, not tiers. @facet handles (i);
# @cast handles (ii). The mesh topology enforces:
#   - Any two substrates X, Y admit a @cast/X/Y species (no privileged
#     path through @cascade linear-descent);
#   - Loss-awareness at every hop (Shannon-loss per Rec #87);
#   - Foerster-gauge preservation as far as translation admits
#     (compile-time refusal at gauge-violating translations per
#     @magic invariant);
#   - Content-address idempotence for round-trip-preserving pairs
#     (Rec #82 β-normal-AST-OID propagation).
#
# The existing 11 `@cascade/code/*/*` species (mirror/gestalt,
# gestalt/gleam, gleam/beam, gleam/js, mirror/gestalt, rust/go,
# rust/llvm, rust/wasm, llvm/turing, purescript/js, turing/mirror,
# formal/prose) map naturally to @cast species during future @cast
# supersession arc: each `@cascade/code/X/Y` becomes `@cast/X/Y` at
# peer-to-peer translation altitude. The @code layer (DELETED
# 2026-08-21 Phase 3b) collapsed into @facet at generation-surface
# altitude; @cascade's translation-between layer lifts into @cast
# (pending future arc; @cascade not yet touched by Phase 3).
#
# === adjunction with @facet ===
#
# When @cast/X/Y is composed with @facet/X and @facet/Y projections,
# the round-trip forms a diagram:
#
#     𝓜 → [@facet/X] → H_X
#     ↓                    ↓ [@cast/X/Y]
#     𝓜 → [@facet/Y] → H_Y
#
# The diagram commutes up to Shannon-loss when @cast/X/Y is loss-
# optimal per @attension. When it commutes strictly (zero-loss), the
# adjunction `𝔕_X ⊣ 𝔛_X ≅ 𝔕_Y ⊣ 𝔛_Y` per Rec #91 amendment §5a
# Theorem 5a.1 lifts to a natural isomorphism between the two facet-
# projections. Substrate-honest reality: most translations are lossy;
# @cast makes the loss measurable and Foerster-gauge-verifiable.
#
# === autopoietic closure at @facet/git ↔ @cast ↔ @facet/mirror ===
#
# The load-bearing operational closure per Rec #91 amendment §8.8
# forward-promise: mirror commits itself to git via @facet/git; @cast
# bridges git-substrate-shape onto mirror-substrate-shape via
# @glue.fold_back(git, mirror) + @fate.tournament(candidates); mirror
# reads git AS itself via @facet/mirror; self-modifies; loop. @cast
# IS the operational carrier of the third-order-cybernetic operator
# that Rec #90 §5 Theorem 5.1 formalizes as `𝓜 = 𝓜(𝓜)` closure at
# runtime altitude.
#
# Spec context:
